# The Codex adapter's settings, read by shim/hansa_codex_shim.py when they are not in its environment (hansa starts
# workers with a clean one). Copy to codex.env, beside this file, and replace each <...>. KEY=VALUE, ~ is the home
# folder. (A trial.env here is read instead while there is no codex.env.)
# The codex program, from an install outside ~/.codex and outside every no-read path of the sandbox:
HANSA_CODEX_BIN=<codex tools>/bin/codex
# The adapter's own CODEX_HOME, holding its login: outside ~/.codex, every no-read path and the worktrees:
HANSA_CODEX_HOME=<adapter's Codex home>
HANSA_CODEX_MODEL=gpt-6.1-sol
HANSA_CODEX_EFFORT=high
# Where each run's JSONL, stderr, thread id and srt settings are kept (default: logs/ beside this file):
# HANSA_CODEX_LOGS=<this folder>/logs
# HANSA_CODEX_SRT=<srt>                   (default: srt on the worker's PATH)
# HANSA_REAL_CLAUDE=<claude>              (default: the first claude on the PATH that is not this shim)
# The certificate file Codex checks TLS against (CODEX_CA_CERTIFICATE): macOS's own check does not complete
# inside srt. Outside every no-read path. Empty: none given.
# HANSA_CODEX_CA_FILE=/etc/ssl/cert.pem   (default: /etc/ssl/cert.pem when it exists)
# The ways to the web that run on OpenAI's side, where srt cannot stop them (README, "The web"). Codex's own web
# search, given as -c web_search=...: disabled (the default), cached or live.
# HANSA_CODEX_WEB_SEARCH=disabled
# Codex features turned off, one --disable each, space-separated; apps closes the codex_apps tools (web_run).
# The default is the list below; empty: none turned off.
# HANSA_CODEX_DISABLE=apps plugins browser_use computer_use image_generation multi_agent hooks
